{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>A Psalm of Asaph. Elohim</b> — the sense of <b>stands in the congregation of El</b>: the Glory that is with the congregation of Israel." "<b>In the midst of Elohim</b> — they are the angels, who are the elohim and the host of heaven, the sons of Elohim, for through the angels come all judgments of Elohim on earth." "And some say: <b>in the midst of Elohim</b> — like: 'Elohim you shall not curse' (Exodus 22:27). And the sense: for He is in their midst, and they must be careful not to judge unjustly."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 82, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:35:47.989516803Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}